<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import LoadMore from './lib/LoadMore.abide'
import loadMore from './lib/LoadMore.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/behaviors/element-size',
        '/behaviors/element-rect',
        '/headless/virtual-list',
        '/reactive/reactive',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/element.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a delivery writes the value, and nothing before it does"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/element.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('elementVisible hands IntersectionObserver its rootMargin and threshold, and is in view from the smallest share",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/reports/lib/TrendOnceSeen.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the trend is drawn when first scrolled to"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Read the older activity when the end of the feed scrolls into view">
        <p>Hand it a function and it is called with each reading. It reads whether the element
            is in the viewport, or inside the element <code>root</code> names.</p>
        <Example code={loadMore}><LoadMore /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Draw the pipeline trend the first time the report scrolls down to the chart">
        <p>Hand it a reactive value and it writes there, holding what you gave it until the
            first reading. Pass <code>once: true</code> and the first <code>true</code> is the
            last thing written. The element stops being observed, so what the value gates
            mounts once and stays mounted when it scrolls away again.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { elementVisible, reactive } from '@abide/abide'

            import PipelineTrend from './PipelineTrend.abide'

            let seen = reactive(false)
            </script>

            <section class="min-h-60" {...elementVisible(seen, { once: true })}>
                {#if seen}<PipelineTrend />{/if}
            </section>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Count a deal as seen once half of its card shows">
        <p><code>rootMargin</code> and <code>threshold</code> are handed to
            <code>IntersectionObserver</code> as it takes them. The element is in view once the
            smallest share <code>threshold</code> names shows.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { elementVisible } from '@abide/abide'

            const card = elementVisible({ threshold: 0.5 })
            </script>

            <article {...card.host} data-seen={card.visible}>Hopper & Co</article>
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
